1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
First, click on the right button in the blank area of the 2D window to set the 2D background, then click on Reset to reset the 2D background.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Before starting the 3D arrangement, we can first organize the 2D panels in the 2D window, such as the parallel panels.

3
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Select the two front panels in the frame, then click on the right button on the panel to select Align, then select Up to align the two panels up and down.

4
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Then go to the 3D tool bar, select Rearrange 2D Arrangement, All, align the panels of the 3D window to the arrangement of the 2D panel.

5
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Next, we will arrange the panels around the virtual model through the arrangement point.

6
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
First, press Ctrl A to select all the panels, then click on the panel, and a positional ball will appear.

7
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,000
In the default situation, the positional ball is targeted at the viewing angle of the screen.

8
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:13,000
In the case of rotating the viewing angle, the three different colors of the X, Y, and Z lines will not be in the same position, and will always remain in the relative position of the lens view.

9
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:21,000
In order to make it easier to use, we can click on the right button in the 3D background to select the positional ball. There are three options here.

10
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Here are the three options.

11
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:32,000
In addition to the screen coordinates that we have just mentioned, there are also partial coordinates and world coordinates.

12
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Partial coordinates are the coordinates of the object itself.

13
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:43,000
For example, here I have a butterfly node from the outside.

14
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:49,000
When I rotate this butterfly node, the positional ball will rotate with it.

15
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
And if we change the positional ball to 3D,

16
00:01:51,000 --> 00:02:01,000
the positional ball will be fixed to the world coordinates.

17
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:06,000
You can choose the appropriate coordinates according to your needs.

18
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Here I choose the partial coordinates.

19
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:18,000
The created panels in the software will use world coordinates, and the models imported from outside will use their original coordinates.

20
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Select all the panels in the software and drag the green line to align the panels to the position of the virtual model.

21
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Or drag the yellow square to align the panels.

22
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Next, go to the virtual model display list in the 3D view menu.

23
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Select the display point and display layout.

24
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:46,000
The green circle around the virtual model is the layout.

25
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
The blue point on the layout board is the layout point.

26
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:57,000
When we select a panel, the mouse will stop at the layout point, which can predict the layout effect.

27
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:04,000
The center of the panel will be placed on this layout point, and then rotate along the layout board.

28
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Click on the layout point to arrange the sleeve panels.

29
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:13,000
You can see that when the panels are arranged, the panels on the other side are also arranged.

30
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,000
If there is a gray circle around the layout point,

31
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:19,000
then this point is the alignment point.

32
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:25,000
When the panels are arranged on the alignment point, the other side of the panel will automatically be arranged.

33
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:33,000
When you turn on the display layout board, you may select the layout board when you click on the panel.

34
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Therefore, in order to prevent non-operational operation, we can turn off the display layout board.

35
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:43,000
When selecting multiple panels, you can place them as a whole in the layout.

36
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,000
Click on the layout board.

37
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Press the Shift key to click on two front panels and place them on the corresponding layout point.

38
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
You can see that the two panels are arranged together.

39
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:00,000
The keys in the 3D window will also react at the same time to the effect after arrangement.

40
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:07,000
We can also separate the front panels.

41
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:11,000
But after arrangement, we will see that the panels are overlapping.

42
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:13,000
You can find the layout in the property editor.

43
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,000
In the property editor, you can find the layout option.

44
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
By adjusting the position of the X-Row and Y-Row,

45
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:24,000
the panels will be separated from each other and adjusted to a position slightly higher than the border line.

46
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
The arrangement option is also set to be symmetrical.

47
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Since we want to sew the border line afterwards,

48
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,000
we must ensure that when the panel is arranged,

49
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:37,000
the following sewing lines will not cause the panel to pass through the body to sew.

50
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Then place the back panel in the appropriate position.

51
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:41,000
By adjusting the position of the panel,

52
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:45,000
the panel will be separated from the model or close to the model.

53
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Adjusting the position of the panel will make the panel no longer intersect with the model.

54
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Then adjust the Y-Row to make the panel line exceed the model.

55
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Then place the pocket in the location of the chest.

56
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,000
When choosing a panel, the mouse is stopped at the point of arrangement.

57
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
It may re-arrange the panel and cause misoperations.

58
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Hence, when we do not need the point of arrangement,

59
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:18,000
The axis of the positioning ball can be pulled out of the pocket of the board to avoid cross-stitching.

60
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:23,000
The 3D arrangement of the board is based on the direction of the 2D window.

61
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:32,000
You can go to the arrangement and direction in the attribute editor to adjust the angle and let the board return to the correct arrangement position.

62
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:41,000
If the board overlaps with other boards and cannot be selected, you can select a board that is blocked and press Shift and Q to hide it.

63
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:47,000
Then drag the axis of the positioning ball to the appropriate position of the pocket board.

64
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Now you can save the project file and prepare to learn the following sewing.

